Greetings!

The penultimate Deck of Souls Early Access update is ready! We're almost at the finish line, and the game will soon enter its full release.

This is your last chance to grab Deck of Souls at a devilish discount, as the price will increase after this update. Do you have what it takes to close the gates of Hell?

https://i.ibb.co/vCNphpV/image.gif

The latest update will include:

 The fourth story chapter;
 A new boss with two phases;
 Two smaller bosses;
 New locations specific to Chapter 4;
 6 new combat encounters;
 7 new random events.

Play Deck of Souls, share your impressions in the Steam discussions and our Discord community, and don't forget to leave a review for the game.

Regards,
Deck of Souls Team

Greetings! 

Thank you to everyone who supported Deck of Souls and played our new demo. We'd love to read about your impressions and ideas, so feel free to post your thoughts in the discussions on Steam or in our Discord.

We've updated the demo a bit, improving some mechanics and fixing a few bugs. 

 Stealth will allow you to avoid debuffs;
 All-round improved map generator;
 Replaced the final node icon on the map;
 Fixed Chinese localization issues;
 Fixed an issue where debuff icons would still display after the previous battle;
 Made minor balancing changes to cards.

Update the Deck of Souls demo to try out the new patch. And don't forget to add the game to your Wishlist! 

Regards,
Deck of Souls Team

Greetings!

The development of Deck of Souls is well underway and progressing smoothly. The Book of Souls is almost complete and will show players an overview of their card collection and overall game progress.

We have also added brand new cards, a discard pile, starter decks for the Rogue and Warrior classes, and four new starter decks for the Caster class (bringing it up to six!).

And we have started work on improving the interface. If you have already played the Deck of Souls demo, we would love to hear your thoughts and ideas about the interface – it will greatly help us. 

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42683012/edde8d0b8bfe78443b8ec097e1768ca698e33e26.jpg
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42683012/f0ef4702f51eb4ec403a616317768f08f0993188.png

There are also several changes to card mechanics:

 Stealth is now lost when dealing damage;
 Snack Attack makes the card instant when in stealth;
 Rush cards are now automatically applied if they are added to the deck and if the Rush value this turn allows it.
 You can no longer draw the same card twice. Once the deck is completely drawn, it will recharge from the discard pile. It's possible to have an empty deck and draw no cards.

We've made the following additional changes:

 Added new cards;
 Cards now display the class they belong to;
 Added mechanics that enable players to discover and search for cards in the deck;
 An indicator to show player damage increases;
 Added effects for cards.

Thank you for supporting Deck of Souls! Join our Discord to share your impressions and chat with other players and the developer. 

Regards,
Deck of Souls Team
